body:
evaluatePlainCondition builds the evaluator context via object spread ({ ...record, data: record }). If record comes from untrusted data, a __proto__/constructor/prototype key can trigger prototype pollution when spreading/assigning into a plain object. Consider building the context on Object.create(null) and copying only safe keys (skipping __proto__/constructor/prototype), then setting data: record.
```suggestion
  // Build a prototype-less evaluation context to avoid prototype pollution from record keys.
  const context: any = Object.create(null);

  if (record && typeof record === 'object') {
    for (const [key, value] of Object.entries(record)) {
      // Skip keys that could lead to prototype pollution
      if (key === '__proto__' || key === 'constructor' || key === 'prototype') {
        continue;
      }
      context[key] = value;
    }
  }

  // Expose the original record under the "data" namespace for expressions.
  context.data = record;

  const evaluator = new ExpressionEvaluator(context, globalCache, globalFormulas);
```

The runtime evaluator supports merging spec rule.style with legacy individual color props (backgroundColor/textColor/borderColor), but SpecConditionalFormattingRule currently only allows { condition, style }. This makes that supported/ tested shape fail TypeScript checks for consumers. Consider adding the optional color props to SpecConditionalFormattingRule (or a shared base interface) so the public types match the supported inputs.
```suggestion
 * Automatically evaluated at runtime via ExpressionEvaluator.
 *
 * Note: Legacy individual color props are supported at runtime and merged into `style`.
 * They remain optional here for backward compatibility.
 */
export interface SpecConditionalFormattingRule {
  /** Plain condition expression (e.g., "status == 'overdue'") or template expression (e.g., "${data.amount > 1000}") */
  condition: string;
  /** Style map to apply when condition matches (e.g., { backgroundColor: '#fee2e2', color: '#991b1b' }) */
  style: Record<string, string>;
  /** CSS-compatible background color (legacy shortcut; merged into style at runtime) */
  backgroundColor?: string;
  /** CSS-compatible text color (legacy shortcut; merged into style at runtime) */
  textColor?: string;
  /** CSS-compatible border color (legacy shortcut; merged into style at runtime) */
  borderColor?: string;
```
